Planex designer_tools — Line 2 real-app evidence (v0.8)
========================================================
Drags are data-driven: what drags is decided by the
AFFORDS graph. The router is ONE rule, zero region
branches, zero hand-wired begins.

[1] drag chip-red (30,22) -> canvas (150,120)...
    red dot at (150,120) — routed by the graph, dropped
    by the commit hook's own region query

[2] drag chip-green (80,22) -> canvas (200,140)...
    green dot at (200,140) — the SAME process, the SAME
    rule; the chip is read from the trajectory

[3] TAP chip-blue (135,22) — no movement...
    tap -> select fired blue (small-displacement commit
    re-compiled through the CLOSURE form — the graph
    decided, the measure arbitrated)

[4] drag chip-blue (135,22) -> canvas (100,160)...
    blue dot at (100,160) — the SAME region, the SAME
    process, a different MEASURE: one region, two acts,
    zero mode flags

[5] click swatch (290,22) — closure-only region...
    select fired on the DOWN (v0.7 semantics, kept
    byte-for-byte for closure-only regions)

[6] drag slider 14 -> 78...
    committed brightness: 78 (preview reads: 40,
    estimate writes during the 42-sample drag: 1)

[7] drag slider 250 -> 70 (the SECOND drag)...
    committed brightness: 70 — the SAME process
    object served its second gesture (the AFFORDS
    edge points at a stable target; reset rearmed it)

[8] press empty space (5,200)...
    no-op: no region there, no handler exists

[9] drag chip-red -> empty space (5,200)...
    gesture committed, no dot — the drop query in the
    commit hook found no canvas under the release

[10] mid-drag cancel (app-side, e.g. an ESC handler)...
    cancelled mid-gesture: no dot, no write, the
    stream released on the next event (reason: "app escape")

Final state: sel=red brightness=70 dots=3
Semantic estimate writes (whole session): 7
Hand-wired begins (px_interaction_* outside the router): 0
Begins compiled through the graph: 8
Raw-coordinate handlers defined: 0 (on_click == NULL)
Unresolved presses (no-op path): 1

=== Line 2 evidence complete ===
ADR-0017/0018 joint obligation (L15b) — what this app shows:
  1. Drags route through the afford graph: 5 regions, 2
     processes, 1 closure, ONE routing rule, 0 region
     branches, 0 hand-wired begins
  2. The begin seam is gone: a down on a process-affording
     region compiles to the process (px_drag_intent embeds
     the label — the value contract, tests/test_v08.c e4)
  3. One graph, two forms: the closure form still serves
     the swatch on the down; the dual chip resolves tap vs
     drag by MEASURE at commit (see tests/test_v08.c f2)
  4. Process reuse: the slider's second drag runs on the
     same object (px_interaction_reset — the stable target)
